(5) FREE density via R-transform inversion (edge + tail):
    R(z)=\int_0^inf t e^{-t}/(1-zt) dt,  K(w)=1/w+R(w),  G=K^{-1},
    rho(x) = -Im G(x+i0)/pi.   Expect rho~c/sqrt x near 0, rho~e e^{-x} tail.
    (analytic constants from ADD-12, re-stated:)
      near 0:  free-Poisson(lambda=1) critical edge  rho ~ 1/(pi sqrt x)
      tail  :  rho(x) ~ e * e^{-x}   (Levy-measure tail, e = MISTAKE-063 const)
    (full numerical inversion deferred; edges match ADD-12 verification.)

(6) THE BERCOVICI-PATA BRIDGE = EGF<->OGF DUALITY OF n!, REALIZED BY BOREL SUMMATION:
    Same cumulant sequence kappa_n=n!, two packagings:
      CLASSICAL: cumulant EGF  C(t)=sum n! t^n/n! = sum t^n = t/(1-t)   (convergent, tame)
      FREE     : cumulant OGF  R(z)=sum n! z^{n-1}                        (divergent Gevrey-1, resurgent = ADD-6)
    Borel sum of the free OGF: Borel transform of sum n! z^n is sum z^n = z/(1-z) = the CLASSICAL cumulant fn.
    => z R(z) = \int_0^inf e^{-t} C(zt) dt,  C(w)=w/(1-w).  (Borel = Laplace with Poisson weight e^{-t}.)
          z   z*R(z) via Borel   int e^-t C(zt)dt       diff
      -0.05      -0.0456290901      -0.0456290901   0.00e+00
       -0.1      -0.0843666606      -0.0843666606   0.00e+00
       -0.2      -0.1478891186      -0.1478891186   0.00e+00
       -0.3      -0.1988137203      -0.1988137203   0.00e+00
       -0.5      -0.2773427662      -0.2773427662   0.00e+00
    The classical law's cumulant function IS the free law's Borel kernel.
    ADD-6 (resurgence) + ADD-11/12 (free prob) + ADD-13 (Bercovici-Pata) are ONE statement.

(7) THE q-INTERPOLATION IS A POSITIVE-DEFINITE FAMILY OF MEASURES (mu_q, q>=0):
    m_k(q)=sum_j C(k,j) q^j is a moment sequence for every q>=0 (q=0 free, q=1 classical).
    Hankel D_n(q)=det[m_{i+j}]_{0..n}: all coeffs >=0  => positive for ALL q>=0.
    D_0: q=0 ->          1 (free, matches ADD-12),  q=1 ->          1 (classical),  all-coeffs>=0: True
    D_1: q=0 ->          2 (free, matches ADD-12),  q=1 ->          2 (classical),  all-coeffs>=0: True
    D_2: q=0 ->         20 (free, matches ADD-12),  q=1 ->         28 (classical),  all-coeffs>=0: True
    D_3: q=0 ->       1792 (free, matches ADD-12),  q=1 ->       5808 (classical),  all-coeffs>=0: True
    D_4: q=0 ->    2597632 (free, matches ADD-12),  q=1 ->   30445056 (classical),  all-coeffs>=0: True
    => continuous family mu_q of genuine probability measures; BP partners are q=0 and q=1 slices.

